\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Euro pedals back up, terrain tough. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,054 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1999\par 12:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 14 (Reuters) - The euro bounced back against the dollar by the European midsession on Wednesday, but remained vulnerable to the pull of lower levels, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  In a nervous market, the euro regained much of its half-cent losses made at the European open, after German "Wise Man" Horst Siebert said his earlier comment that the euro could fall to $0.90 was not a serious forecast. \par \par \uc2  "Siebert's back-pedalling has taken us up," said Jeffrey Woodruff, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BankBoston. \par \par \uc2  "We will get to parity, but not necessarily in the next week," he added. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $1.0164/68 at 0954 GMT, from earlier lows of $1.0126 and from a life low of $1.0104 hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen also recovered to 122.93/04 from lows of 122.56, just above the life low of 122.53 set on June 18, when the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought euro/yen for the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The twin threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength and to bolster the euro was providing some support for Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "A move to parity will increase speculation of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Geraldine Concagh, economist at AIB Group Treasury in Dublin. \par \par \uc2  Further weakness in euro/yen, meanwhile, was likely to encourage \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Woodruff said the dollar/yen low of 120.50 set on June 21 might trigger further Bank of Japan yen sales. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen fell to its lowest level on Wednesday since the Bank of Japan sold yen for dollars on July 5. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the dollar/yen exchange rate was trapped on Wednesday between moves in euro/dollar and euro/yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 121.01/06 at 1005 GMT, from a low of 120.90 and from 121.26/31 in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Argentina remained a bugbear for the dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Worries that Argentina would default on its debt weighed on the dollar in New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar recovered after Argentina's ruling party's presidential candidate Eduardo Duhalde denied calling for Argentina's debt to be pardoned. \par \par \uc2  But the market would remain on alert for further political statements from Argentina, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The market was also watching U.S. producer price and retail sales data for June, to be released at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "They will confirm strong non-inflationary growth, which could put further pressure on the euro," said Concagh. \par \par \uc2  Producer prices are forecast to rise by 0.1 percent month-on-month and 0.2 percent year-on-year, while retail sales are expected to gain 0.3 percent on the month and 1.0 percent on the year. \par \par \uc2  Sterling's recovery from the day's lows against the dollar tracked euro/dollar moves, but was aided by a fall in British unemployment to a 19-year low in June. \par \par \uc2  British average earnings in the three months to May rose a slightly-above-forecast 4.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  The pound was trading at $1.5568/73 at 1020 GMT, from a low of $1.5515 and from $1.5578/88 in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the pound strengthened to 65.34/37 pence from 65.41/44 late on Tuesday. ((Carolyn Cohn, 