\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr slips as BOJ stays out,eyes on Kuroda-Geithner. \b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1999\par 08:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO July 14 (Reuters) - The dollar eased by late afternoon Tokyo trade on Wednesday, having edged lower in the absence of any dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also pressured indirectly by sales of euros for yen by foreign operators in the afternoon, as well as firmness in Tokyo share prices. \par \par \uc2  The market was focusing on a meeting between U.S. Treasury Undersecretary for International Affairs Timothy Geithner and senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda later on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 121.06/11 yen as of 0604 GMT, compared with 121.25/35 yen in late New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro stood at $1.0156/63 as of 0615 GMT, compared with $1.0171/76 in late New York. "The theme in the market was whether the BOJ would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  following rises in the yen overnight," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Traders said some dealers bought dollars earlier, speculating that the BOJ might do the same. But such dealers later squared their positions as there were no signs of BOJ action, they said. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda said on Wednesday morning a premature strengthening of the yen would be undesirable for the Japanese economy. Kuroda also said Japan was ready to take decisive action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also watching for potential BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros for yen. Dealers were mindful of the fact that the BOJ started buying euros for yen last month after the fledgling European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below 123 yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros for yen via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 18 after the euro fell to a record low of around 122.60 yen. The BOJ again bought euros for yen on June 21. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at 123.09/22 yen as of 0623 GMT, compared with 123.40 yen in late New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The meeting between Geithner and Kuroda was being watched for possible signs of discord between the United States and Japan. \par \par \uc2  "Dealers have been interpreting recent comments by Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers in a negative way," as a sign of disagreement between Japan and the U.S. on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, said a dealer for another city bank. \par \par \uc2  Summers said last week that Tokyo should focus on economic fundamentals rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. "Manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not the approach that leads to long-term prosperity," Summers said in a television interview last Wednesday. But some dealers said the Geithner-Kuroda meeting may not yield any fresh trading incentives. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt that Geithner would have anything negative to say about (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  right after a meeting with Japanese authorities. I think the meeting may come and go uneventfully," the first city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A government source said Geithner and Kuroda were likely to meet after 4 p.m. or possibly 5 p.m. (0700 or 0800 GMT). \par \par \uc2  In the near term, dealers said, there would be some focus on the June U.S. producer price index, due for release at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast on average that the PPI would show a rise of 0.1 percent month-on-month, both for the overall figure and that excluding food and energy prices. \par \par \uc2  The PPI could become a catalyst for a fall in the dollar if it fuels concerns about inflationary pressures, but dealers said any impact was likely to be limited as the market was preoccupied by the potential for more dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ. The euro fell late in Tokyo afternoon against both the dollar and yen after a foreign newswire reported that German "wise man" Horst Siebert said the possibility of the euro falling to 90 cents should not be excluded. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the report spurred euro selling by U.S. fund operators. The euro fell as low as 122.80 yen and $1.0134 as of 0651 GMT. ((Masayuki Kitano, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7e04l36\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
