\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr steady vs yen in Tokyo amid caution over BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 776 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1999\par 06:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 14 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady against the yen at midday in Tokyo on Wednesday, having failed to break out of a tight range amid expectations that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the yen's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Latin America jitters have waned after Argentina's ruling party presidential candidate on Tuesday denied ever calling for the nation's debt to be forgiven, but the dollar's upside was likely to be limited before the release of key U.S. price data. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 121.29/31 yen at 0310 GMT, compared with 121.25/35 yen in New York late on Tuesday. The euro was at $1.0174/77, versus $1.0171/76 in New York. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday in overseas markets, the dollar slipped as low as around 121.14 yen and $1.0210 to the euro as the Dow Jones Industrial Average briefly fell more than 100 points on fears of a possible Argentine debt default. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained ground by late New York trade, as the Dow trimmed losses by the close to end down 25.96 points or 0.23 percent at 11,175.02. \par \par \uc2  The Dow reversed course after Eduardo Duhalde, the ruling Peronist Party's presidential candidate, reversed his earlier stance on Tuesday by saying he would not seek forgiveness for Argentina's debt. \par \par \uc2  But some dealers said jitters over Latin America could remain as a potential risk factor for the dollar ahead of Argentina's presidential election on October 24. \par \par \uc2  "There is a possibility that U.S. PPI and CPI data due out this week will have some impact on Latin America markets," said Hank Note, senior vice president at Sumitomo Bank. \par \par \uc2  "If Latin American markets are shaken again, then there is likely to be a repercussion in the U.S. markets," he said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. producer price index (PPI) for June will be released at 1230 GMT on Wednesday and the consumer price index (CPI) for June at 1230 GMT on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the risk of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was brewing as the dollar neared its low of 120.90 yen seen on July 5 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the dollar aggressively. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters on Wednesday that a premature strengthening of the yen would be undesirable for the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  He added that Japan was ready to take decisive action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary. Dealers said the market was wary that the BOJ might also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the euro against the yen if the euro slips below 123 yen. \par \par \uc2  "A number of stop-loss sell orders are likely to be triggered if the euro dips below 123 yen, a move that could drag the dollar/yen rate sharply lower as well," Sumitomo's Note said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 123.40/45 yen at 0330 GMT, compared with 123.40 yen in New York late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also wary ahead of a meeting between Kuroda and visiting U.S. Treasury Undersecretary for International Affairs Timothy Geithner. \par \par \uc2  A government source declined to give a specific time for the bilateral talks but said the two are likely to meet after 4 p.m. or possibly 5 p.m. (0700 or 0800 GMT). \par \par \uc2  Neither side has any plans to hold a briefing after the talks, the source said. \par \par \uc2  "After (U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence) Summers recently criticised BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market is carefully watching whether there is any discord between Japan and the United States over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy or not," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Summers said last week that Tokyo should focus on economic fundamentals rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. "Manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not the approach that leads to long-term prosperity," Summers said in a television interview last Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was stuck in a tight range between $1.0168 and $1.0180 on Wednesday morning in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  It dropped to a fresh lifetime low of $1.0108 in late Tokyo trade on Tuesday after the German Federal Statistics office said retail sales fell a real 2.8 percent in May year-on-year. But the euro briefly rose above $1.02 overnight partly on vague talk that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support it against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said that any ECB euro-buying, if true, was probably due to reserve adjustments rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7e04kxh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
