\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's Sakakibara says  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  indispensable. \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1999\par 20:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's influential former vice finance minister for international affairs, Eisuke Sakakibara, said Wednesday that government \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are an indispensable tool in an imperfect market, The Nihon Keizai Shimbun (Nikkei) reported. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara, in an interview on Nikkei's Thursday edition, said "Prices are ultimately set by the market, but the market is not perfect. The government has a role - not opposing the market, but complementing it," noting that "\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are one way of doing this." \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara retired from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 8. His successor, Haruhiko Kuroda, has already made it clear that he will continue Sakakibara's basic policy stance. \par \par \uc2  "With globalization and the spread of the virtual economy," Sakakibara said, "the market will inevitably overreact at times, so smoothing out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations is necessary." \par \par \uc2  "When an overreaction occurs, it's vital to hold a dialogue with the markets and correct it," he said. "Leaving everything to the markets will cripple capitalism." \par \par \uc2  According to Sakakibara, Japan's recent economic situation is reminiscent of 1993 and 1994. At that time, capital spending was rebounding and stocks climbing, but a sharp upturn in the yen set back economic recovery by at least one year. Based on that experience, he said, the ministry has been conducting "preventive" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't mean to suggest that exports should be expanded through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but can the economy recover smoothly if the dollar suddenly hits 115 yen or 110 yen?" he asked. \par \par \uc2  ((New York Japan Desk: 212-859-1760)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7e04fky\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
