\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Lower But Recent Ranges Intact \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 1999\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar was lower Monday in Asia than its levels late Friday in New York, as expectations of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  went unfulfilled and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained wedged in its recent ranges. \par \par \uc2  The dollar reached an early intraday high against the yen of Y122.53 at 0005 GMT on speculation that the Bank of Japan would begin the week with a strong signal to markets that premature yen strength would not be tolerated ahead of an economic recovery. The BOJ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on three of the last four Mondays to sap the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  Some market participants also thought that recent personnel changes at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would provide the timing for some market direction. Monday marked the start of Haruhiko Kuroda's first full week in his new position as vice finance minister for international affairs, and some wondered if he would have some especially strong comments. \par \par \uc2  However, such expectations proved unfounded. No BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ensued, nor did Kuroda even have any remarks for reporters upon his arrival at the ministry. The dollar's gains were gradually pared down to an intraday low of Y122.08 at 0153 GMT, after which it bobbed back up and down on small waves of interbank position adjustments. \par \par \uc2  "(Government officials) have no complaints (with dollar-yen) at this level," noted Hajime Sato, assistant general manager of the treasury department at Daiwa International Trust Bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0510 GMT (1:10 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y122.16, below 122.38 late Friday in New York and down from 122.41 late Friday in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0191, higher than $1.0180 late Friday in New York and above $1.0188 in London Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0530GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1074 1863 28038 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7c05a5f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
