\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Tokyo Volatilities Slightly Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 1999\par 05:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by Japanese yen and euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options are slightly higher in Tokyo Monday compared with Friday's late New York levels, amid so far unfulfilled anticipation that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot trading would break out of recent ranges. \par \par \uc2  The dollar reached an early intraday high against the yen of Y122.53 at 0005 GMT, as some market participants wondered if Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  personnel changes would lead to a new direction for the market. \par \par \uc2  Some wondered if Haruhiko Kuroda's first full week in his new position as vice finance minister for international affairs would begin with a show of force in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on three of the last four Mondays to sap the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  However, no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ensued, nor did Kuroda speak to reporters upon his arrival at the ministry. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ has no reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are stable, for the most part, and volatilities continue reflect this," a Tokyo city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options imply volatility of 9.75% bid, up from 9.5% in New York Friday, and above 9.65% in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, remained above its new low of $1.0146 against the dollar, which it reached on Thursday. While the Asian session has so far seen narrow range-trading between $1.0185 at 0144 GMT and $1.0193 at 2132 GMT, dealers said new lows are possible this week as the euro inches its way toward parity with the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "In the long term, people are still talking about parity more than they're talking about any (euro) recovery," the city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, volatilities are higher at 9.4% from 9.3% in New York Friday. Euro/dollar options were quoted at 9.35% in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 0345 GMT, the dollar is at Y122.23, down from Y122.38 late Friday in New York. The euro is at $1.0189, up from $1.0180 Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Risk-reversals favor dollar yen call options against dollar puts at\par 0.3%, and euro puts against dollar calls at 0.2%, dealers said.\par Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call\par options by the premium or discount applied.\par   -By Lisa Twaronite, 813-5255-2929; ltwaronite@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-07-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0356GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7c059xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
