\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Fairly Steady, Seen Staying Range-Bound \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 1999\par 02:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar is steady against the yen in early Tokyo trading Monday and is expected to move in a relatively narrow range during the Asian session, as it is still squeezed by two countervailing forces in a quiet, directionless market. \par \par \uc2  "I expect the dollar to move in a range of Y122.00-Y122.80 today, caught between offers from Japanese exporters and institutional investors in the high Y122s and bids from other Japanese investors and U.S. investment trusts around Y122," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is quiet this morning as market participants are cautious about possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on three of the last four Mondays, so there is some cautiousness in the market. But I don't think the BOJ will come in today. The dollar is steady above Y122.00 and the euro is unlikely to fall below Y123.00, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last time," a dealer at a Japanese city bank said. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are also awaiting possible remarks this morning on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese monetary officials such as Haruhiko Kuroda, newly appointed vice finance minister for international affairs. \par \par \uc2  At 0005 GMT (8:05 p.m. EDT Sunday), the dollar was trading at Y122.40, almost unchanged from Y122.38 in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at Y122.62 late in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $1.0193, above $1.0180 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.0219 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0015GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7c059gh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
