\par\par \b \uc2  Kuroda says to maintain Japan policy to curb yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1999\par 08:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 9 (Reuters) - Japan's new top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, pledged on Friday to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of his predecessor Eisuke Sakakibara. At a news conference with the new and just-retired vice finance ministers for international affairs, Kuroda reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets to block a premature yen rise. \par \par \uc2  "We are not thinking of a specific range (for dollar/yen). But in order to curb excessive market movements, we will engage in a dialogue with the market and, as needed, take action," Kuroda said. "We don't have any specific figures in mind." \par \par \uc2  Asked how he would differ from the outspoken Sakakibara, dubbed "Mr Yen" for his sway over the markets, Kuroda said: "As needed, I will send a signal to the market, or take action." \par \par \uc2  Asked if MOF would continue with the yen-selling market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it has conducted five times since the government released strong economic growth figures on June 10, Kuroda said: "As we have often said, a premature strengthening of the yen is unfavourable for the Japanese and world economies." \par \par \uc2  The most favourable thing was for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reflect economic fundamentals and move in a stable manner, he said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability was desirable for Japan's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda sidestepped a question about comments by new U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "manipulation" was not the way for Japan to achieve economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda, who has publicly charged the United States with having an inconsistent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy over the years, said the Group of Seven's united stance on the importance of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability remained firm. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara added that he was sure Summers did not mean by his comments that he thought \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices in its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Asked about Kuroda, Sakakibara said with his characteristic cackle: "Although he looks like a nice guy, I think in fact he will be tougher as vice minister than I." \par \par \uc2  Asked about his own future, Sakakibara acknowledged there was much talk about what he would do but that he planned to consider his options while fulfilling his new position as adviser to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He has been offered a visiting professorship at the Australian National University and has reportedly also been offered a position at Keio Univesity in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "New Vice Minister Kuroda will take centre stage to do his work now," Sakakibara said. "I will be on the sidelines or working behind the scenes. I have exited the stage." ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8022 email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7904ugg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
