\par\par \b \uc2  TOCOM gold ends lower on BOE auction, platinum up. \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 09:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 7 (Reuters) - Yen-based gold futures ended sharply lower on Wednesday, tracking a slide in New York overnight triggered by a disappointing auction by the Bank of England (BOE), traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Spot gold prices dropped more than expected, and that pulled down the futures," said a commodities brokerage analyst. \par \par \uc2  The British \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctioned 25 tonnes of gold on Tuesday, as part of a plan to unload 415 tonnes of gold to help balance its portfolio. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume was relatively heavy, with buying on dips by individual investors as the distant contracts breached 1,000 yen per gram, while trading houses engaged in arbitrage trade, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Gold futures ranged from 19 to 23 yen per gram lower. Benchmark June ended down 21 yen at 992 yen, hitting a new life-of-contract low. \par \par \uc2  Spot gold was quoted at $255.60/6.10 at 0721 GMT, against $256.60/7.10 overnight in London. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the dollar was confined to an extremely tight range in late afternoon trade in Tokyo amid nervousness over possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  Platinum futures opened weaker on softer spot prices, but gained in afternoon trade as some trading houses covered short positions, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Platinum futures closed slightly firmer across the board, ranging from two to 13 yen per gram higher. Benchmark June ended four yen higher at 1,298 yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said funds continued to shift from platinum group metals to the gasoline and kerosene futures launched on Monday, lured by active trading and heavy volume. \par \par \uc2  Palladium contracts ended mixed, ranging from eight yen per gram lower to five yen higher. Benchmark June ended down four yen at 1,176 yen. \par \par \uc2  Silver futures ended mostly lower on weaker spot prices. \par \par \uc2  The contracts ranged from 3.0 yen per 10 grams lower to flat. Benchmark June ended down 1.4 yen at 194.5 yen. ((Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431 tokyo.commodit.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv770516x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
