\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Euro yet to win market confidence. \b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 17:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 7 (Reuters) - The euro bobbed in narrow ranges against the dollar on Wednesday, holding above its recent life low, but failing to find a toehold above the $1.0250 barrier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro was undermined in the afternoon by rumours, swiftly denied, that the Green Party was about to leave Germany's coalition government over a nuclear energy dispute. \par \par \uc2  Stronger-than-expected German manufacturing orders and narrowing yield spreads between 10-year U.S. T-notes and German Bunds did nothing to boost the euro, analysts noted. \par \par \uc2  "It's all a confidence game right now," said Michael Rottmann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Hypovereinsbank in Munich. \par \par \uc2  "The spread between U.S. T-note and German Bunds yields has significantly narrowed over the last three weeks and euro zone economic data are improving, but it doesn't help the euro and it is very frustrating." \par \par \uc2  The 10-year spread was currently at 125 basis points, around 50 basis points below the peaks seen in mid-June. When spreads were last at this level the euro was trading at around $1.07. \par \par \uc2  But at 1430 GMT on Wednesday the battered single unit stood at $1.0223/27, little changed from Tuesday's late European levels and around 0.5 percent above the life low of $1.0180 hit yesterday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also well bolstered against several other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most significantly against sterling and the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  The pound fell to a new 33-month trough of $1.5560 on Wednesday and was last at $1.5589/94 compared with $1.5745/55 late in Europe on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Sterling broke yesterday two very big chart supports," said a trader at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "With interest rates favouring short positions in sterling and long positions on the dollar, I expect at least a five percent fall (in sterling) in the short-term." \par \par \uc2  Traders said they were awaiting the decision of the Bank of England's Monetary Policy Committee on rates on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts were expecting British repo rates to be left on hold at 5.0 percent, the same levels U.S. fed funds are currently at. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile euro/sterling was struggling to push higher having earlier reached 65.73 pence, its highest level in nearly a week. It was last at 65.53/55 from 64.93/95 late in Europe on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc, the first \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to suffer in the most recent bout of dollar strength, was at 1.5678/88 francs against an eight-year peak of 1.5740 hit late on Tuesday trade. \par \par \uc2  Despite the dollar's current vigour, technical analysts said signs pointing towards a mild stabilisation in euro/dollar indicated that a fall towards parity would not be so swift. \par \par \uc2  "We are starting to see some divergences on the charts which signal a slowing in the downward trend for euro/dollar," said Simona Soci, technical analyst at Standard and Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  She added that a cluster of support levels was building up between levels just below parity and $1.0030/40. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, wariness that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to aid the euro if it approached parity was enough to temporarily mitigate the vehemnce of dollar bulls. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile dollar/yen remained glued to the 122 area, with dealers still worrying about possible market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar was last at 122.14/19 yen from 122.33/38 in late Europe on Tuesday. Euro/yen was at 124.88/92 compared with 125.05/15 in Europe on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Haurhiko Kuroda said overnight Japan was watching dollar/yen and euro/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates more closely than in the past. \par \par \uc2  "People are still concerned about Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or the possibility of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on their behalf," said Bank of America's economist Robert Hayward. \par \par \uc2  ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets 0171 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7704yzu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
