\par\par \b \uc2  Japan gold investment seen tied to yen strength. \b0\par\par\uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 13:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 7 (Reuters) - Japanese gold investors are waiting for the yen to strengthen against the dollar and push yen-based prices lower before indulging in a buying spree, industry officials said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "When speaking about yen-denominated gold, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations become key... Otherwise, spot prices would have to fall drastically to have an effect on the price of gold in Japan," a bullion house official said. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, spot bullion was quoted at $256.00/6.40 at 0844 GMT, down slightly from the overnight London close of $256.60/7.10. \par \par \uc2  The closing price in London was a fresh 20-year low marked after the Bank of England (BOE) unloaded the first 25 tonne parcel of the 415 tonnes it plans to sell on the market to help balance its portfolio. \par \par \uc2  Some officials said that, at current prices, the yen would have to strengthen to about 118 to the dollar in order to attract investors, as that would push the retail price of the precious metal below 1,000 yen per gram. \par \par \uc2  "There could be some demand if the retail price breaches (the low of) 1,042 yen marked last month, but a significant boost would be difficult without breaking below 1,000 yen," another bullion house official said. \par \par \uc2  Industry officials, however, were divided on when the dollar/yen rate was likely to weaken enough to encourage gold investment. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in recent days supporting the dollar, so it looks like it will take a bit longer for gold prices to fall below 1,000 yen," the second official said. \par \par \uc2  On June 11, yen-denominated gold hit its lowest retail price in 23 years at 1,042 yen per gram, as the global price tumbled in the wake of the BOE's controversial announcement that it planned to cut its gold holdings by more than half. \par \par \uc2  The record low retail price for gold in Japan was 1,040 yen, marked on September 3, 1976. \par \par \uc2  Demand for the precious metal rose among investors who intend to hold gold for the long term, with purchases amounting to about eight tonnes during the two weeks after the British \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement, an official at the World Gold Council in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese investment demand hit a record high of 150 tonnes in 1995, when the dollar slid below 80 yen and domestic retail prices tumbled to 1,050-1,060 yen. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Japan's retail price of gold was at 1,059 yen per gram, while the premium to London spot prices in Tokyo was offered at around 65 cents per ounce, bullion house officials said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was confined to a tight range in late afternoon trade in Tokyo amid nervousness over possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars. ((Ayumi Moriyama, Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431 tokyo.commodit.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7704y2e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
