\par\par \b \uc2  ECB Noyer: Sees Euro Recovery On Fundamentals - Nikkei \b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 05:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--The euro should strengthen as euro-zone countries' economies improve in the second half of this year, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice-president Christian Noyer said in an interview published in Japan's Nihon Keizai Shimbun Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets undervalue the euro, and it should go higher," Noyer was quoted as saying. "Europe's economy has reached bottom, and toward the second half of this year it will grow," he added. \par \par \uc2  He cited rising exports and a recovery in consumption as reasons behind the economic improvement. \par \par \uc2  Noyer also said that there is little possibility that the ECB will change its monetary policy, as both interest rates and industrial prices are at appropriate levels. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's request that the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on its behalf on June 18 to support the euro against the yen "was gladly received, as it did not go against the ECB's policy," Noyer said. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0300GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv77053vs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
