\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Euro hits record low as Noyer fails to warn. \b0\par\par\uc2  By George Nishiyama \par \uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 1999\par 10:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 6 (Reuters) - The euro dipped to a record low against the dollar on Tuesday in Tokyo, falling prey to speculative sales and as a visiting European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  senior official refrained from any strong warning against the fall. \par \par \uc2  "We have stated that we are not interested in a weak euro," ECB Vice President Christian Noyer told a Tokyo symposium as the euro slid to an all-time low in late Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  "I am absolutely confident that euro will be a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the international markets," Noyer added. \par \par \uc2  But in the absence of any more robust statement against the euro's ongoing fall, it dipped as low as $1.0184. \par \par \uc2  It was standing at around $1.0218/25 as of 0810 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Noyer even appeared to play down the euro's weakness since its birth this year, saying the depreciation was partly a reaction to the rise of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the euro-zone countries in the last few months of 1998 in anticipation of its launch. \par \par \uc2  "What happened after January 1 is that the euro went back to its original position," Noyer said, adding that it "more or less reflected fundamentals" taking into account the exchange rate between the dollar and the euro-zone \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 1997 and 1998. \par \par \uc2  But on the euro's outlook, Noyer was optimistic, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "firmly based on internal price stability" and that he and the ECB governing council agree that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "has a clear potential for a stronger external value", repeating the words of his boss, ECB President Wim Duisenberg. \par \par \uc2  Noyer also reiterated that member states of the Growth and Stability Pact are committed to maintaining fiscal balance or even fiscal surpluses in the medium term, denying a rumour that circulated in Tokyo earlier on Tuesday that euro-zone countries would drop their three percent budget deficit targets. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers also said the absence of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the euro against the yen accelerated the speculative sales of the euro. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Eisuke Sakakibara, also speaking at the symposium, had ironically earlier praised the ECB for "efficient" implementation of its euro-buying, yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month on behalf of the BOJ. ((George Nishiyama, Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv76053pm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
