\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Euro/dollar feeble near new life lows. \b0\par\par\uc2 706 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 1999\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 6 (Reuters) - The euro remained under pressure against the dollar in European trading on Tuesday after falling to new life lows under $1.02 in the wake of talk in Asia that euro-zone budget deficit limits could be relaxed. \par \par \uc2  Although European officials have begun trying to talk up the euro and many analysts expect an eventual turnaround, the market appeared to be focusing on the $1.00 level for now, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "There will be bids and stops at every round levels along the way - $1.0150 next, then $1.01. So it won't be a straight line, but it seems clear we're gradually headed toward parity," said Yuji Tashiro, a dealer at Daiwa Europe Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0215/20 at 0805 GMT after dipping to a new life low of $1.0186 earlier on Tuesday. That compares with $1.0221/23 late in Monday's European session. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer said at a symposium in Tokyo that he was "absolutely confident" that the euro would be a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but his remarks did little to rescue the embattled euro. \par \par \uc2  David Brickman, economist at PaineWebber in London, said the euro's weakness was also a result of the market's bullishness on the U.S. economy after the Federal Reserve raised interest rates and removed its tightening bias last week. \par \par \uc2  "That's boosted the other side of the equation of the euro (against the dollar)," he said. \par \par \uc2  "When later in the year we do actually start to see evidence of, firstly, a pick-up in growth in Europe and, secondly, a slowdown in the U.S. economy, the euro will start to turn around," he added. "In the very short-term, markets are very focused on the likelihood of stronger U.S. growth." \par \par \uc2  In Asian trading overnight, the euro was hit by an article in Monday's German daily Handelsblatt saying a French planning commission supervised by premier Lionel Jospin had proposed a relaxation of the euro zone's budget deficit limits. \par \par \uc2  Although the story fuelled concerns in Asian trading, European traders were less worried by the report. \par \par \uc2  "The rumours got blown up out of all proportion overnight, and if this is all it is, I would completely dismiss it," said a trader at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Brickman at PaineWebber forecast European officials' attempt to support the euro verbally would intensify as euro/dollar neared parity. He added there was a rising risk that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/yen to forestall broad yen gains. \par \par \uc2  "With the (euro's) lows again, there is a severe risk of a Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 124.73/84 yen after falling as low as 124.29 earlier in the session from 125.05/15 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Fear of BOJ action underpinned the dollar against the yen, keeping the greenback glued near 122 yen. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at 121.96/10 yen against 122.33/38 yen late on Monday. Persistent selling interest from Japanese exporters and hedge funds kept the topside limited. \par \par \uc2  "The problem in Japan is that we are not seeing a genuine recovery at the moment and Japanese authorities are determined to keep the yen reasonably soft," PaineWebber's Brickman said, noting economic data out of Japan lately had remained mixed. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Tuesday showed Japan's diffusion index of leading indicators rose to 64.3 in May from 55.6 in April and household spending rose 2.4 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, Japanese Trade Minister Kaoru Yasano said overnight the tankan business survey report released on Monday showed corporate capital expenditure was not improving. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, sterling floundered near a 23-month low against the dollar in the wake of the euro's weakness. Sterling was at $1.5694/04 from $1.5745/55 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling appreciated against the euro, with euro/sterling trading at 65.07/13 pence from Monday's 64.93/95. ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv76053nb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
