\par\par \b \uc2  Euro plumbs new depths vs dollar as BOJ stays out. \b0\par\par\uc2 633 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 1999\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 6 (Reuters) - The euro hit a fresh lifetime low against the dollar in late Tokyo trade on Tuesday as active speculative sales in euro/yen triggered stop-loss sales of the euro against the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said speculative sales in euro/yen intensified in late trade as the Bank of Japan (BOJ) refrained from stepping into the market to stem the yen's rise against the euro. \par \par \uc2  In early trade, the euro came under pressure against the dollar and the yen on vague rumours that the nations in the euro zone might relax strict budget deficit limits. \par \par \uc2  At 0653 GMT, the euro stood at $1.0190/95 after dipping as low as $1.0184. It was at $1.0228/32 in late Europe on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped to as low as around 124.25 yen following the late rounds of speculative sales. It had stood at 124.53/64 yen against 125.10 yen in Tokyo at 0000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "Relatively heavy stop-loss sales in euro/yen dragged down the euro against the dollar. The euro is vulnerable to active sales now as its basic sentiment remains weak," a Japanese city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the afternoon, comments by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) Vice President Christian Noyer briefly lifted the euro off its lows against the dollar and the yen. \par \par \uc2  In a Tokyo symposium on the euro, Noyer said that he is confident the euro will be a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in international markets, repeating that the ECB was not interested in a weak euro. \par \par \uc2  Noyer also said that member states of the Growth and Stability Pact are committed to maintaining fiscal balance or even fiscal surpluses in the medium term. \par \par \uc2  The rumours about a relaxation of the budget deficit criterion by euro-zone nations induced speculative sales of the euro led by overseas operators, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down especially against the yen in the morning. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the dollar crawled near a day's low near 122 throughout the day in dull trade, but the market was wary about selling it too strongly below 122 yen due to possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a high of 122.40 yen but then faded as follow-through bids by speculators failed to emerge in the face of offers from exporters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  An Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumoured placing offers near 123 yen to protect its knockout options orders placed around that level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Speculators who had earlier built up long positions on the belief that the BOJ would buy dollars again gradually unwound their positions after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed away. \par \par \uc2  But the market lacked the energy to trade dollar/yen actively after Monday's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  Stop-loss offers were rumoured to be placed around 121.80 yen but firm dollar bids were detected above that level. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary officials continued to talk down the yen, which added to market nerves, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, chief of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Bureau, said the ministry is ready to take appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, repeating that a premature strengthening of the yen was undesirable. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda is scheduled to be appointed Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday had been aimed at pre-empting a premature rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted through the BOJ, Miyazawa told a regular news conference: "A premature yen rise is troubling so they acted to pre-empt it." ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv76053ll\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
