\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr eases near low vs yen, but market wary of BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 1999\par 06:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 6 (Reuters) - The dollar had crawled near a morning session low against the yen by Tokyo midday on Tuesday, but the market was wary about selling it too strongly below 122 yen due to possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro stood barely above its life low of $1.0200 and was under downward pressure against the dollar and the yen on vague rumours that the nations in the euro zone might relax strict budget deficit limits. \par \par \uc2  At 0335 GMT, the euro stood at $1.0216/26 against $1.0225/28 at 0000 GMT in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese city bank dealer said the rumours induced speculative sales of the euro led by overseas operators, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down in thin trade, especially against the yen. \par \par \uc2  But active follow-through sales were limited as operators were unsure of the origin of the rumour. \par \par \uc2  The market was also cautious about driving down the euro while the threat of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/yen remained. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was support for the euro at $1.02 and 124.50 yen. At 0341 GMT, it stood at 124.66/89 yen compared with 125.10 yen in Tokyo at 0000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  At 0346 GMT, the dollar stood at 122.02/09 yen compared with 122.32/37 in late European trade. U.S. financial markets were closed for a market holiday on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a high of 122.40 yen but then faded as follow-through bids by speculators failed to emerge in the face of offers from exporters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Speculators who had earlier built up long positions on the belief that the BOJ would buy dollars again gradually unwound their positions after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed away. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar was drifting down without BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but selling pressure is not strong as it was after previous rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in June)," a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "A wait-and-see mood is persisting today. Operators were unwilling to sell the dollar aggressively below 122 yen." \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary officials continued to talk down the yen, but active yen sales were limited, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, chief of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Bureau, said on Tuesday the ministry is ready to take appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, repeating that a premature strengthening of the yen was undesirable. \par \par \uc2  "A premature strengthening of the yen is undesirable for the Japanese economy. We are also ready to take decisive and appropriate action in the markets," Kuroda told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda is scheduled to be appointed Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday had had been aimed at pre-empting a premature rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted through the BOJ, Miyazawa told a regular news conference: "A premature yen rise is troubling so they acted to pre-empt it." \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the market detected the BOJ stepping in to sell yen shortly after the release of the quarterly "tankan" survey of business sentiment. The BOJ was spotted buying dollars at levels as high as above 122.50 yen on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to move in a tight range in the afternoon. Many operators will seek direction from a Tokyo seminar on "The euro: its promise and challenge to the world economy", which starts at 0430 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister Eisuke Sakakibara, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer, and Germany's former Vice Finance Minister Heiner Flassbeck will attend the seminar. ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7605371\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
