\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS-Euro on defensive vs yen, wary over BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 1999\par 05:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 6 (Reuters) - The euro was pushed below 125 yen by mid-morning in Tokyo on Tuesday, but found support on the downside as the market remained wary the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said a substantial volume of sell orders from exporters was thought to have been lined up above 125 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Their (exporters') selling interest on rallies is still very strong," said a trader at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0221 GMT, the euro stood at 124.78/96 yen, compared with around 125.07 yen late in Europe on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. market was closed for the Independence Day holiday on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro edged down as low as 124.63 yen in morning trade. \par \par \uc2  It had shot up more than one and a half yen to 125.71 yen on Monday from 123.96 yen in late New York on Friday, in tandem with the steep rise in dollar/yen after the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars and sell yen. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the euro was unable to maintain its gains as profit-taking appeared, and was expected to remain under strong downward pressure on continuing euro-selling interest by exporters and hedge-related sales by investors. \par \par \uc2  If a stop-loss point at 124.45 yen was triggered, it could take the euro back to 122.63 yen, a lifetime low set on June 18 before the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros and sell yen. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the euro was easier versus both the yen and the dollar on a market rumour that a European media report said euro zone nations may drop the target of cutting budget deficits to three percent of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  "If euro/yen falls further, we certainly see a risk of another BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday morning, the head of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Bureau, Haruhiko Kuroda, said the ministry is ready to take appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, repeating that a premature strengthening of the yen was undesirable. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, said he would not make any further comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Kuroda is to be formally appointed to replace Sakakibara as vice finance minister for international affairs on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, German Economics Minister Werner Mueller said worries about the weakness of the euro were unfounded from a long-term point of view, but his remark had little impact on the market. \par \par \uc2  At 0430 GMT, the Institute for International Monetary Affairs will hold a seminar in Tokyo on "The euro: its promise and challenge to the world economy". \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer, and Germany's former Vice Finance Minister Heiner Flassbeck will attend. \par \par \uc2  German June jobless data is scheduled for release at 0800 GMT on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, sterling was at 192.19/31 yen, little changed from 192.15 yen in late Europe. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss Franc stood at 77.69/74 yen versus 77.91 yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-1396, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv76052xw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
