\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Lower As BOJ Leaves Market Alone \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 1999\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell slightly against the yen Tuesday from its late Monday levels in London, as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  disappointed many market participants by failing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push up dollar-yen further in Asia trade. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ's failure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again today to push up the dollar disappointed a lot of market players who had been expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer at a Japanese city bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has been trapped in a relatively narrow range of Y122.00-122.40 so far in the Asian session, caught between offers from Japanese exporters and option holders above Y122.50 and fears of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  below Y122.00. With Monday's latest round of Bank of Japan dollar-buying still fresh in market participants' minds, market players were wary of testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve. \par \par \uc2  These market participants received a warning from Japan's current international bureau head and soon-to-be vice finance minister for international affairs Haruhiko Kuroda. \par \par \uc2  "An excessive yen strengthening before economic recovery is undesirable," he said, adding, "We will take decisive action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at any time." \par \par \uc2  With the New York markets closed for a national holiday Monday, Tokyo dealers were divided over how the U.S. market would react to the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push up the dollar Monday. While some thought U.S. players may sell the dollar to take profits, others felt the dollar might rise further in the short-term as long as the dollar stayed above the Y122.00 level Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y121.98, below Y122.34 late Monday in London. The dollar was at Y122.55 late in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0218, lower than $1.0223 late Monday in London Monday. The euro was at $1.0223 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y124.64, down from Y125.07 in London late Monday. The euro was quoted late in Tokyo Monday at Y125.33. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5753, even with $1.5753 in London late Monday. Sterling was at $1.5762 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0530GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 28038 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv760521u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
