\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS-Euro up on tankan, BOJ yen sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1999\par 06:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 5 (Reuters) - The euro was firmer against the yen by Tokyo midday on Monday as yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) weakened the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and on somewhat weaker-than-expected Japanese economic data. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's quarterly "tankan" survey of business sentiment showed the big manufacturers' diffusion index improving to minus 37, compared with minus 47 in the previous survey. \par \par \uc2  That was slightly lower than a Reuters consensus forecast of minus 36. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed Japan had entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "A premature strengthening of the yen's exchange rate is not appropriate. Today we took action in the market," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro's upward momentum picked up, especially after breaking 124.50 yen, the level at which major stop-loss orders were placed. \par \par \uc2  The euro briefly extended gains above 125 yen, but was unable to maintain its gains as speculators quickly unwound their positions to take profits, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0305 GMT, the euro was at 124.80/85 yen compared with about 123.96 yen in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the weaker-than-expected tankan results, the basic yen-buying mood remains intact because the results were not weak enough to suggest a change in the current general yen-buying trend," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  "It's only the BOJ who is forcing down the yen, but the market is clearly not following that force," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BOJ was first seen buying dollars at between 121.50 yen and about 121.80 yen. It was later detected buying dollars above 122 yen, and as high as about 122.30/40 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro/yen rate would follow dollar/yen, but the euro was expected to remain under strong downward pressure on rallies on continuing euro-selling interest by exporters, and hedge-related sales by investors. \par \par \uc2  European investors were rumoured to be bidding the yen to invest into the Japanese equity market. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) board member Eugenio Domingo Solans said on Friday the Federal Reserve's monetary policy would not influence the monetary policy of the 11-nation euro zone. \par \par \uc2  "If we had an exchange rate target, they would (affect ECB policy), but that is not the case," he told a seminar. \par \par \uc2  "We watch it (the exchange rate) in terms of its influence on inflation but we don't have a target for the exchange rate." \par \par \uc2  The yen weakened across the board, in line with its weakness against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc was quoted at 77.71/76 yen compared with around 77.22 yen in late New York trade on Friday. Sterling stood at 192.30/42 yen versus 190.83 yen on Friday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-8785, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv75059r8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
