\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  meant to guard economy-MOF Tanami. \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1999\par 10:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 5 (Reuters) - Japanese Vice Finance Minister Koji Tanami said on Monday that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) earlier in the day was meant to prevent negative impact on Japan's economy from a premature rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Tanami told reporters the government was prepared to take "appropriate action" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Asked about reasons for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, Tanami said: "We are concerned that premature strength in the yen would have negative effects on the nation's economy. We are taking action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with that stance." \par \par \uc2  The government wanted to ensure that signs of recovery in the real economy, which had been detected in Japan's gross domestic product (GDP) in the January-March quarter and the Bank of Japan's "tankan" corporate survey, would lead to a recovery in private-sector activity. \par \par \uc2  "In the meantime, we want to take action to avoid moves in financial markets, such as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stock or bond markets, that would have a negative impact (on the economy)," Tanami said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan said on Monday its June tankan survey produced a minus 37 reading for large manufacturers, up from the minus 47 in March. It was the second consecutive improvement. \par \par \uc2  GDP for the January-March quarter stunned markets by rising 1.9 percent from the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2  ((Yoko Nishikawa, Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv75051y6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
