\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF acted in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market on Monday-Kuroda. \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1999\par 02:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 5 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) took action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, senior MOF official Haruhiko Kuroda told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose above 122 yen after the Bank of Japan (BOJ) announced its "tankan" corporate sentiment survey, which showed that the big manufacturers' diffusion index improved to minus 37 compared with minus 47 in the previous survey. The index was slightly lower than a Reuters consensus forecast of minus 36. \par \par \uc2  It was not clear whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came before or after the tankan's release at 8:50 a.m. (2350 GMT on Sunday). \par \par \uc2  "A premature strengthening of the yen's exchange rate is not \par \par \uc2  appropriate. Today we took action in the market," Kuroda said. \par \par \uc2  Traders had been wary since the start of trading on Monday that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the market took the yen higher after the "tankan" showed brighter prospects for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , coupled with stop-loss dollar purchases induced after the "tankan" came in slightly weaker than expected, thrust the dollar above 122 yen in early trade. ((Tokyo newsroom +813-3432-8018 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv75051j1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgo