\par\par \b \uc2  OPTIONS -  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  vols soften before long U.S. weekend. \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1999\par 19:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, July 2 (Reuters) - Implied volatilities for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  options softened slightly as the dollar showed little inclination to retest Thursday's sharp gains against the euro and Swiss franc ahead of the long U.S. holiday weekend. \par \par \uc2  One-month euro/dollar option vols slipped to 9.5/9.65 percent from 9.55/9.8 percent on Thursday when the euro/dollar fell to a lifetime low of $1.0201. \par \par \uc2  The cash euro/dollar spot rate recouped losses above $1.02450 on Friday on expectations that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by buying euros and selling yen, traders and dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Eisuke Sakakibara on Friday declined to comment on overnight rumours of yen-selling, euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was carefully watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, particularly euro/yen rates, which have moved rapidly recently. \par \par \uc2  One-month euro/yen vols popped up to 11.45/11.75 percent on such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters, flattening out the curve from one-month to one-year euro dollar vols, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  option dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't provide you with a reason to buy the long end," one dealer said about euro/yen options vols. "But talk of it has caused the front end to move up with the long end." \par \par \uc2  Despite speculation the BOJ may buy euros for yen, one-and two-month euro/dollar risk reversals still favoured euro puts by midday on Friday. One-month 25-delta risk reversals were at 0.2/0.4 and three-month euro risk reversals stood at 0.1/0.3. \par \par \uc2  Three-month euro risk reversals remained in euro call territory, trading at flat/0.1, while one-years are trading with a euro call bias of 0.2/0.3. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/yen risk reversals are still showing a bias for yen calls as traders expect the BOJ's quarterly "tankan" survey of business sentiment will confirm that the Japanese economy is rebounding. \par \par \uc2  Vols for one-month dollar/yen eased a touch to 10.5/10.7 percent from 10.5/10.8 percent on Thursday, while one-year vols slipped to 12.15/12.35 percent on Friday against 12.4/12.6 percent. \par \par \uc2  Three-month dollar/yen vols traded slightly firmer at 11 percent versus about 10.85 percent 24 hours ago, they said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  options activity is expected to dwindle on Friday afternoon. IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures closed at 1200 CDT/1700 GMT Friday ahead of the U.S. Independence Day holiday. All U.S. markets will be closed on Monday. ((Chicago Derivatives Desk(312)408-8750 chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv720591a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
