\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar moves little vs yen, but cautious on BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1999\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 2 (Reuters) - The dollar was stuck in a narrow range against the yen at the Tokyo midday on Friday, but drew support from lingering speculation of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should its downtrend accelerate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar remained under strong downward pressure as holders of long positions, taken in anticipation of BOJ dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were eagerly looking for a chance to unwind those positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved in a narrow range of 120.73 to 120.98 yen in morning trade. At 0321 GMT, it was quoted at 120.90/96 yen compared with 120.78/88 yen in late New York trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Market players are unwilling to take new positions now before Monday's 'tankan' data and tonight's U.S. jobs data," a Japanese commercial bank dealer said. "Many operators still want to push down the dollar, but apparently they are sidelined." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Japanese public funds were rumoured to be lining up bids around 120.50 yen. Trust banks and other institutional investors were also rumoured to be placing bids. \par \par \uc2  The euro remained under downward pressure, with sales of euro/yen indirectly weighing on dollar/yen. But operators were cautious about driving down the euro too aggressively after comments by Japanese Vice Finance Minister Eisuke Sakakibara. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara told reporters on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was carefully watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, particularly euro/yen rates, which have moved rapidly recently. \par \par \uc2  He declined to comment, however, on overnight rumours of yen-selling, euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro got a lift overnight on rumours that central banks were selling yen for euros. Dealers said they had heard talk of the Bank of Japan checking rates of the euro against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) and other central banks declined to comment overnight. \par \par \uc2  A European bank dealer in Tokyo said rumours of rate checks by the BOJ spread when the euro was around 123.50 yen and pushed it up to around 124.80 yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the overnight rally, some U.S. banks were detected selling the euro below 124 yen this morning. They seemed to be doing the selling for Japanese investors," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But the market was very careful about selling too aggressively, especially after Sakakibara's comments," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect downward pressure on the euro could pick up speed if it breaks below 123 yen again, given Japanese investors' interest to liquidate further. \par \par \uc2  "We've spotted Japanese investors liquidating some positions in the euro on rallies. Some of them were even selling European bonds recently," a Japanese brokerage trader said. \par \par \uc2  "I wouldn't be surprised to see them stepping up their efforts if the euro's downtrend accelerates." \par \par \uc2  At 0347 GMT, the euro was quoted at 123.74/79 yen compared with about 123.88 yen in Tokyo at 0000 GMT. The euro was at $1.0235/45 against $1.0226/29 in late New York trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar/yen was expected to move in tight ranges ahead of U.S. jobs data later on Friday and the tankan. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters expected, on average, that U.S. non-farm payrolls rose 220,000 in June after an 11,000 gain in May. The unemployment rate was seen unchanged at 4.2 percent and average hourly earnings were forecast to have risen 0.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  And 18 economists projected on average that the tankan index for big manufacturers would improve a hefty 11 points to minus 36, while forecasts ranged from minus 41 to minus 27. ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv72056yj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
