\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS - Euro propped up by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1999\par 04:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 2 (Reuters) - The euro was marginally higher against the yen by midday in Tokyo cross trade on Friday on short-covering and profit-taking after tumbling overnight. \par \par \uc2  Although the euro retained a weak bias against the yen, speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese or European authorities stemmed its decline. \par \par \uc2  "Long positions have been wiped out after the overnight losses. Sentiment is bearish, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears are preventing dealers from building fresh shorts," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  As of 0201 GMT, the euro was quoted at 123.67/76 yen compared with an overnight low around 123.50 yen hit in late New York trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Offers from Japanese investors were detected near 124 yen, dealers said, while stop-loss sell orders were thought to be lurking slightly below 123.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was carefully watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, particularly euro/yen rates, which have moved rapidly recently. \par \par \uc2  Rumours of euro-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight briefly lifted the European unit. \par \par \uc2  "I think there was a strong possibility that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred overnight, judging from price movements. Such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely aimed not to lift the euro, but to keep it from plunging," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  There was also talk that the Bank of Japan (BOJ) was checking euro rates near 123.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Asked about overnight rumours of euro buying against yen, Sakakibara said: "No comment." \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) and other central banks overnight declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk. \par \par \uc2  Dealers do not expect the euro to deteriorate sharply against the yen. \par \par \uc2  If the euro does fall, monetary authorities will likely step in but it would most likely occur in early European time, when the market has more liquidity, a dealer at a Japanese commercial bank said. \par \par \uc2  The ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) on June 18, after the euro fell to a lifetime low of 122.63 yen, and on June 21. \par \par \uc2  The euro also dropped sharply against the dollar overnight, hitting a lifetime low of $1.0200. \par \par \uc2  German Economics Minister Werner Mueller said on Thursday the ECB is rightly obligated to protect price stability but was also required to support the economy. He added that the latest ECB rate cut has created more room for expanded investment. \par \par \uc2  The ECB governing council decided on Thursday to leave its key refinancing rate unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Separately, ECB governing council member Yves Mersch said short-term movements in the euro's value should not be confused with long-term trends. \par \par \uc2  Mersch said there was no discussion and no comment about the euro's renewed slide at Thursday's ECB meeting. \par \par \uc2  He added that the ECB's view remained that the euro has potential to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  "There is a general impression that the ECB is not overly concerned about a weak euro because it helps support the economy," a dealer at a trust bank said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Swiss franc was quoted at 77.05/10 yen compared with around 76.97 yen in late New York trade on Thursday. Sterling was at 190.20/32 yen versus 189.92 yen in New York. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-8027, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv72056vk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
