\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar rangebound vs yen, tone stays weak in Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1999\par 09:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  At 0638 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 120.70/80 yen compared with 121.17/22 yen in late New York trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Many operators are still forecasting a strong-yen senario in the future. But wariness over possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is limiting aggressive sales," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "All the market needs is another convincing signal on the outlook of the Japanese economy." \par \par \uc2  BOJ Policy Board member Kazuo Ueda said on Thursday that Japan's economy was likely to remain weak and that more time was needed before deflation fears abated. \par \par \uc2  It is too early to discuss a further easing of monetary policy, Ueda said, adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its current policy until deflationary fears subside. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reacted little, but his comments boosted the key 10-year Japaense government bond futures price more than one point and pushed down long-term cash JGB yields sharply. \par \par \uc2  The action in dollar/yen was limited throughout the day, but dollar-selling interest continued to limit the upside. \par \par \uc2  "Major Japanese exporters were spotted moving their sell orders for dollars lower to around 121.50 yen and below," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese life insurers and securities firms were also spotted placing offers slightly above 121 yen. \par \par \uc2  Although many sell orders were detected, the market would need more incentives to drive down dollar/yen rates in the near term, with the focus on National Association of Purchasing Management data later in the day and U.S. jobs data on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Some tension in the U.S. asset markets was lifted after the Fed adopted a neutral bias after the FOMC, but we still need to monitor the pace of the U.S. economy very closely," the European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Fed, as expected, ended a two-day policy meeting on Wednesday by pushing the federal funds rate up one quarter of a percentage point to 5.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro edged up to $1.0366/70 as of 0719 GMT, from $1.0353/56 in New York on Wednesday. Light short-covering emerged in Tokyo ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (ECB) monetary policy meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  heading lower against the dollar was the Swiss franc, which has been in a long decline as the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  grapples with a weak economy by cutting rates and encouraging a depreciation to make exports more competitive. \par \par \uc2  Overnight the Swiss franc sank to its lowest level since August 1991 at 1.5566 per dollar. Although it bounced lightly in Tokyo, dealers said a test of the 1991 trough at 1.5937 appeared inevitable. \par \par \uc2  At 0727 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 1.5466/76 Swiss francs, against 1.5488/98 in late New York trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Commodities and commodity-related \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also gained as the Fed's modest move seemed to pose no threat to the U.S. economy or to a recovery in world growth. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar broke through tough resistance around 66.50/60 U.S. cents and was quoted at 66.90/67.00 as of 0727 GMT compared with 65.90/95 on Wednesday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7105d28\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\p