\par\par \b \uc2  ECB-Yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  entirely settled by BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1999\par 16:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, June 29 (Reuters) - The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday that its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was entirely settled by the Japanese side and thus did not show in Tuesday's ECB financial statement. \par \par \uc2  The ECB said in a footnote to its regular weekly financial statement that its purchase of euros against yen on June 18 was done entirely on the account of the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  "These transactions were settled directly by the Bank of Japan and did not therefore affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings of the Eurosystem," the ECB said. \par \par \uc2  The statement appeared to be saying that the ECB used Japanese money for the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that the transaction would show up in the Bank of Japan's foreign reserve holdings only. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank president Tietmeyer also said last week he was not sure the term "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " was appropriate for the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  as according to his definition \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  required two parties. \par \par \uc2  "This was one-sided, however. The European System of Central Banks (ESCB) acted upon request of another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that's a very normal procedure," Tietmeyer said. \par \par \uc2  Had the ESCB used some of its own holdings, the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have figured in the financial statement for the week ending June 25 and not the previous week's as it takes a few days to process such transactions. ((Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525, frankfurt.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6t05hf1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
