\par\par \b \uc2  POLL-BOJ tankan seen improving, economy still weak. \b0\par\par\uc2      By William Mallard \par \uc2 901 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 1999\par 08:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2     TOKYO, June 28 (Reuters) - Pessimism among Japan's businesses \par \par \uc2  is likely to have dissipated markedly over the past three months \par \par \uc2  but the improvement does not mean the economy is out of the \par \par \uc2  woods, a Reuters survey of economists finds. \par \par \uc2      Economists uniformly expect improvement for a second \par \par \uc2  consecutive quarter in the Bank of Japan's "tankan" survey of \par \par \uc2  business sentiment, but they caution that the economy remains \par \par \uc2  weak and some fret that bullishness is running ahead of reality. \par \par \uc2      The tankan is drawing closer attention than usual after an \par \par \uc2  unexpectedly strong economic surge reported earlier this month. \par \par \uc2      The BOJ has also suggested that the tankan, which will be \par \par \uc2  released at 8:50 a.m. on July 5 (2350 GMT on July 4), may be a \par \par \uc2  key clue for monetary policy. \par \par \uc2      In forecasts compiled by late Friday, 18 economists projected \par \par \uc2  on average that the tankan index for big manufacturers would \par \par \uc2  improve a hefty 11 points to minus 36, while forecasts ranged \par \par \uc2  from minus 42 to minus 20. \par \par \uc2  The tankan sentiment gauge is a diffusion index of the \par \par \uc2  percentage of companies reporting favourable business conditions \par \par \uc2  minus those reporting unfavourable conditions. A negative reading \par \par \uc2  means pessimists outnumber optimists. \par \par \uc2  Although the forecasts were below zero, they all showed \par \par \uc2  improvement from the March survey reading of minus 47, which had \par \par \uc2  been the first upturn in nearly two years. \par \par \uc2  Similarly, the forecast for big non-manufacturers was on \par \par \uc2  average minus 26, an eight-point rise from the last tankan, with \par \par \uc2  forecasts ranging from minus 35 to minus 18. \par \par \uc2  The average forecast of minus 36 for manufacturers nearly \par \par \uc2  matched the projection of minus 38 the companies themselves made \par \par \uc2  in March for the June tankan. \par \par \uc2      The survey average of minus 26 for big non-manufacturers was \par \par \uc2  also little different from the minus 27 the firms had forecast. \par \par \uc2      Some of the economists suspect their forecasts may be too \par \par \uc2  conservative in the wake of January-March gross domestic product \par \par \uc2  data, reported on June 10, which showed the economy grew at an \par \par \uc2  annualised rate of 7.9 percent from the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2      The bullish undercurrent is reflected in Tokyo share prices, \par \par \uc2  which are up by one-third from their January lows for the year. \par \par \uc2      Indeed, some in the market speculate that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the muscular yen against \par \par \uc2  the dollar and the euro were pre-emptive moves to stave off a yen \par \par \uc2  rampage on an unexpectedly strong tankan. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami himself drew attention to the \par \par \uc2  upcoming tankan on June 16 when he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \par \par \uc2  scrutinise the poll for clues as to whether a threat of deflation \par \par \uc2  remains. Deflation fears have become the BOJ's litmus test for \par \par \uc2  whether to maintain its policy of guiding short-term interest \par \par \uc2  rates essentially to zero. \par \par \uc2  Tomoichiro Nakamaru, chief economist at Commerz Securities \par \par \uc2  and a touch more bullish than average in his forecasts, said \par \par \uc2  factors such as the strong GDP data and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  implied an upside risk for sentiment. \par \par \uc2      "It wouldn't be strange if there were a positive surprise," \par \par \uc2  Nakamaru said. \par \par \uc2      On the other hand, Andrew Shipley at Schroder Securities \par \par \uc2  Japan noted that companies cut their industrial production \par \par \uc2  forecasts for both April and May. Such downward revisions signal \par \par \uc2  that the tankan will come in weaker than the companies had \par \par \uc2  forecast in the previous survey. \par \par \uc2      "Clearly, the risks are that people are getting too upbeat \par \par \uc2  about business sentiment in Japan," Shipley said. \par \par \uc2      The 18 economists also forecast, on average, that the tankan \par \par \uc2  would find companies planning to cut capital spending by 7.7 \par \par \uc2  percent in the business year to next March, less severe than the \par \par \uc2  9.4 percent cutback the companies reported in the previous \par \par \uc2  tankan. The 18 forecasts for spending cuts ranged from six \par \par \uc2  percent to nine percent. \par \par \uc2  The economists in the Reuters survey were split on what the \par \par \uc2  tankan might say generally about the economy, which the \par \par \uc2  government says has stopped worsening but has not clearly begun \par \par \uc2  to recover. \par \par \uc2  HSBC Securities Japan said the tankan would show the economy \par \par \uc2  has hit bottom, while Nikko Salomon Smith Barney said the survey \par \par \uc2  "should confirm that the economy has yet to trough". \par \par \uc2  The following are the results of the Reuters survey of \par \par \uc2  economists on the sentiment of large manufacturers and \par \par \uc2  non-manufacturers and for capital spending by 