\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Denies  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Will Harm U.S. Cooperation On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 798 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1999\par 04:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market won't hurt U.S.-Japan cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said Friday. \par \par \uc2  Japan has come under increasing international pressure to revive its sluggish economy, mired in its deepest recession since the end of World War II. Japan's economy is still struggling to shake off the effects of a plunge in land prices in the early 1990s, which buried the country's banks under a mountain of failed or risky loans. \par \par \uc2  Japan has bought $15 to $20 billion in the dollar-yen market alone this month, selling its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 10, 14 and 21. In addition, the Bank of Japan had the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchase euros on its behalf June 18 and bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own last Monday in a bid to stop the yen's advance. \par \par \uc2  Although recent government data indicate signs of improvement in Japan's economy, the nation is still struggling to overcome its worst recession since World War II. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are seen as an attempt to ensure the emerging recovery is not damaged by the yen's sudden surge. \par \par \uc2  A strong yen would make Japanese exports -- the main engine of the economy -- more expensive abroad and thus potentially hamper the economy's ability to recover from recession. That's why the Bank of Japan sold yen on June 10, when it reached a seven-week high near 117.50 to the dollar on a report showing Japan's unexpected economic growth in the January-to-March period. \par \par \uc2  Asked at a regular press conference about a report that the U.S. officials have been making dismissive comments about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Miyazawa said, "I haven't heard of such a report. I doubt that it is a fact. Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't hurt cooperation between \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy." \par \par \uc2  Asked whether he was referring to the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future, Miyazawa said, "What I meant isn't joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Regarding the idea of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  underwriting government bonds, Miyazawa said he sees no need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do so. "My position (on the issue) hasn't changed. There is no need for the BOJ to underwrite the bonds." \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami has consistently rejected calls to underwrite bonds as a measure to help the economy, although some ruling Liberal Democratic Party politicians continue to suggest the measure. \par \par \uc2  Asked when the Japanese government would review the overall tax system, Miyazawa said, "As I have repeatedly said in parliamentary sessions, I think it desirable to review the overall system when the economic recovery is firmly in place." \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, said that there is no change in the Japanese government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and that the government's resolve is very strong. Speaking to reporters upon entering his office, Sakakibara said, "There is no change in our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. Our resolve is very firm," said Sakakibara, whose knack for influencing exchange rates earned him the moniker "Mr. Yen." \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara added that the U.S. and Japan, and Europe and Japan are cooperating on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  very well. \par \par \uc2  On a related note, the head of the international bureau at Japan's Finance Ministry said that the government has never had an upward limit in mind for the dollar's exchange rate against the yen. "There has never been a ceiling," Haruhiko Kuroda told a small group of reporters. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda was asked whether Sakakibara's remark meant that the government has no ceiling in mind for the dollar-yen exchange level. Kuroda also said that there is no change in the cooperation between Tokyo and Washington in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Taichi Sakaiya, the head of Japan's Economic Planning Agency, said that the Japanese government would judge whether or not extra measures are needed to support the economy based on an overall assessment in September. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a regular press conference, Sakaiya said the government would consider closely the gross domestic product, or GDP, figures for the April-to-June quarter and will make an overall assessment. Japan's GDP figures -- the total market value of goods and services produced in the country -- are set for release in September. \par \par \uc2  Asked if he was concerned that public-works spending would peter out in the second half of the year, Sakaiya said that the government would think of extra measures only if it became clear that public works were running out of steam. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329dv6p02y69\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
