\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Slightly Higher Vs Yen In Narrow Bands \b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1999\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar wallowed around Y122 for most of Thursday's Asian session, ending a tad above its levels late Wednesday in New York as fear of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  offset selling pressure from overseas players and Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was lower against the euro compared with its levels in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, Japanese vice finance minister for international affairs, let \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers know early in the session that he is still keeping a close eye on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying just enough to keep memories of recent BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fresh. \par \par \uc2  "We are watching the dollar/yen and the yen/euro very carefully," Sakakibara said. \par \par \uc2  With the BOJ having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  so frequently in recent sessions, some short-term speculators bought the dollar aiming to ride it higher if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to sell yen. But those expectations weren't realized, and the dollar's topside was limited by selling from overseas funds and by Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ wasn't in the market today, so the dollar's topside was limited," said Shuji Takano, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ABN AMRO Bank in Tokyo. "Most people feel that once the BOJ stops \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar's topside will be limited." \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y121.97, slightly higher than Y121.95 late Wednesday in New York but basically unchanged from Y121.98 late Wednesday in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0338, higher than $1.0333 late Wednesday in New York and higher from $1.0310 in London Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0530GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 28038 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6o04pix\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
