\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-Japan flexible on dlr above Y125-Utsumi. \b0\par\par\uc2  By George Nishiyama \par \uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1999\par 11:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 23 (Reuters) - Japanese authorities appear to have become more flexible in allowing the dollar to rise above 125 yen, Makoto Utsumi, former Japanese vice minister for international affairs, said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Utsumi told Reuters in an interview he believed the authorities wanted a buffer against a premature strengthening of the yen. \par \par \uc2  "They are more flexible on the dollar rising beyond 125 yen," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said they probably were hoping two to three weeks ago that the dollar would move within a range of 115 yen to 125 yen. \par \par \uc2  "But seeing the (recent) bullish sentiment for the yen, they want to have more of a buffer," he added. \par \par \uc2  Utsumi said he does not think Japanese authorities have a specific range in mind for the dollar/yen rate now, adding that it was very difficult to define where to "advance and retreat" while one was fighting against strong market sentiment. \par \par \uc2  On the issue of cooperation between Japanese and U.S. authorities in the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (BOJ) recent yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar, he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not have been possible if the U.S. had been strongly opposed to it. \par \par \uc2  He also said the BOJ's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro, carried out through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB), was ground-breaking as it showed that a new era of a tri-polar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system among the dollar, the yen and the euro had been established. \par \par \uc2  "(The ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the BOJ) in essence can be called a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It will make it easier for future coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  On the outlook for the Japanese economy, Utsumi, now a professor at Tokyo's Keio University, said the economy was likely to achieve the government forecast of 0.5 percent growth for this fiscal year, which runs until March 2000. \par \par \uc2  Following the release of stronger-than-expected gross domestic product (GDP) data for the January-March quarter, Utsumi said, "It is very clear that we would achieve (0.5 percent growth) and more." \par \par \uc2  He listed strong housing sales, expected demand for new durable goods to replace old goods, and the recent firmness in Tokyo share prices as bright spots in the economy. ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6n0601o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
