\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar ends US down giving back dramatic gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1999\par 23:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 23 (Reuters) - The dollar closed mostly lower, giving up its dramatic gains against several European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as American asset markets slipped amid fears U.S. interest rates may rise more sharply than investors expected. \par \par \uc2  By the close, the euro had swung to gains and stood at $1.0337/42, comfortably above its $1.0277/79 open and the all-time low of $1.0254. At the same time British pound recovered to end at $1.5806/11 from $1.5765/75 as the dollar fell to 1.5455/65 Swiss francs from 1.5522/32. \par \par \uc2  The dollar lost ground against the yen and ended at 121.88/98 after opening at 122.07/17. \par \par \uc2  The close, dealers agreed, painted a dramatically different picture than the open where the market was bracing for more dollar gains against the British pound, the Swiss franc and most likely the euro. \par \par \uc2  Even before the New York open, the dollar had hit a 21-month high against the British pound as traders interpreted a report from the Bank of England to suggest more interest rate cuts may be on the way. \par \par \uc2  It was also trading at an eight-year high against the Swiss franc after having surged past 1.5520 francs. So a new lifetime low for the euro, below $1.0254 seemed within reach. \par \par \uc2  "Basically the weak euro - fuelled by soft growth expectations for the region - was the trigger for the dollar to catch up and post gains versus the Swiss franc and the British pound," ING Barings Capital senior vice president John McCarthy explained. \par \par \uc2  But soon jitters about the chance for quick-paced U.S. interest rate hikes felled both the U.S. bond and stock markets and subsequently curbed the dollar's robust gains. \par \par \uc2  "The momentum was simply not there anymore and there had been talk of large order buying as the euro traded near $1.0290," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Speculation the Federal Open Market Committee, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate setting arm, may lift rates by more than the quarter percentage point most dealers have discounted helped send Treasury yields still higher on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "People are very nervous and don't want to be holding big positions. The Dow and Treasury prices fell and that was enough to pull the dollar lower again," a dealer at a U.S. investment bank explained. \par \par \uc2  Treasury yields jumped past the the psychologically key level on Tuesday and inched higher on Wednesday. The Dow Jones industrial average fell 54.77 points to 10666.86. \par \par \uc2  The euro swung to gains in the wake of the Dow Jones industrial average's loss and as Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's cabinet approved a wide-ranging economic reform plan aimed at shedding 30 billion marks of state budget costs in 2000. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the gains were assured after stops were hit near the $1.0320 level. Now they are setting their sights on resistance near $1.0370. If that breaks, dealers are optimistic that $1.0450 may be reached and that a short-term bottom has been set for the euro. \par \par \uc2  As the euro inches higher, fears that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also eased. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may was absent for the second consecutive day after having sold yen aggressively four times in the last three weeks. "Right now that is not so much of an issue, it would become more of a problem again if the dollar slipped to 121.50 or lower," the dealer at the investment bank said. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar rose against the Canadian dollar to C$1.4713/23 from C$1.4690/00. ((-Svea Herbst-Bayliss, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1638 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6n05sve\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
