\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar/yen drips lower as dollar/Swiss skims 1.54. \b0\par\par\uc2 175 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 11:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0944 GMT - Dollar/yen trickles down to 121.60 support as dollar/Swiss nears 1.54 prop. Market wary of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after rhetoric overnight. Euro/dollar firm, near $1.0360 cap, euro/yen off lows. German Finance Ministry sees signs of recovery growing, expects to hit 1999 growth forecast. MOF's Sakakibara said weaker yen acceptable if needed for recovery. \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  FinMin Miyazawa said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at pre-empting unjustified yen rise, not boosting economic growth. \par \par \uc2  * South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy dollars. South Korea Finance Ministry official had overnight expressed concern about the won's strength vs yen and said was closely watching dlr/yen impact on local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  * Swedish crown eases from earlier record high vs euro, record reached for fifth consecutive trading day. \par \par \uc2  * Bank of France's Trichet speaks on euro at 1630 GMT. \par \par \uc2  * UK Chancellor of Exchequer Brown attends House of Lords committee hearing on MPC at 1445 GMT. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6m06054\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard